# REQUIRES: lean
#
# A verdict that rests on a Lean proof rests on what its module uses, as a
# solver's does: callee contracts and spec facts. Certification runs before
# those are settled, whatever else failed, and a certified result gets the
# qualifiers and vacuity checks of a verified one.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t.backend %t.termination %t.mixed %t.inductive
#
# The Lean backend, with every goal proved. An export proves nothing, so it
# runs no vacuity check.
# RUN: %cpp-verify --backend=lean --no-lean-auto --lean-project=%t.backend %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_backend.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BACKEND-EXPORT
# RUN: sed -i.orig 's/^  sorry$/  trivial/' %t.backend/CppVerify/Proofs/*/*.lean
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_seven.lean %t.backend/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_seven_634ea3/cppverify_seven_634ea3_postcondition_f0d135e6.lean
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_trusting.lean %t.backend/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_trusting_b6301a/cppverify_trusting_b6301a_postcondition_bafafdfb.lean
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_impossible.lean %t.backend/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_impossible_9d6c7c/cppverify_impossible_9d6c7c_postcondition_1cd35301.lean
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_same.lean %t.backend/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_same_9601c2/cppverify_same_9601c2_postcondition_ce92acf8.lean
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_positive.lean %t.backend/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_positive_fb6abf/cppverify_positive_fb6abf_postcondition_78bdd643.lean
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=lean --no-lean-auto --lean-project=%t.backend --lean-certify %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_backend.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BACKEND
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=lean --no-lean-auto --lean-project=%t.backend --lean-certify --diagnostics-format=json %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_backend.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BACKEND-JSON
#
# The same project with an admitted lemma: nothing is certified, and what the
# vacuity checks found goes with the verdicts.
# RUN: echo 'theorem admitted : True := by sorry' >> %t.backend/CppVerify/User.lean
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=lean --no-lean-auto --lean-project=%t.backend --lean-certify %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_backend.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BROKEN
#
# A generated check that is quiet when proved is reported when certification
# fails.
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --backend=lean --no-lean-auto --lean-project=%t.inductive --lean-certify %S/Inputs/inductive_unproved.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INDUCTIVE
#
# A spec's termination proved in Lean, beside a function that fails: first
# with the proof left as sorry, then completed.
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --solver-rlimit=1000 --lean-fallback=%t.termination %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_termination.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EXPORT
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --solver-rlimit=1000 --lean-fallback=%t.termination --lean-certify %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_termination.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SORRY
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_termination.lean %t.termination/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_scaled_decreases_52d363/cppverify_scaled_decreases_52d363_termination_3164b050.lean
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --solver-rlimit=1000 --lean-fallback=%t.termination --lean-certify %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_termination.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PROVED
#
# A function proved by Z3 and Lean together establishes its contract, and
# its result is qualified as a solver's is.
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --solver-rlimit=300 --lean-fallback=%t.mixed %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_mixed.cpp --
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_mixed.lean %t.mixed/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_product_4751c3/cppverify_product_4751c3_postcondition_c4d4674b.lean
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_looping.lean %t.mixed/CppVerify/Proofs/cppverify_looping_3f4bd4/cppverify_looping_3f4bd4_postcondition_d06fccd0.lean
# RUN: not %cpp-verify --solver-rlimit=300 --lean-fallback=%t.mixed --lean-certify %S/Inputs/lean_dependencies_mixed.cpp -- 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED

# A contract without a definition establishes nothing, whoever proves the
# caller.
# BACKEND: Unresolved: seven [backend=Lean] [reason=callee.contract] (relies on the contract of next (no definition;
# BACKEND: Certified: trusting [backend=Lean] [trusts=assumed]
# BACKEND-NEXT: Certified: impossible [backend=Lean] [vacuous]
# BACKEND-NEXT: warning: impossible: the precondition is unsatisfiable, so every claim about it holds vacuously
# BACKEND-NEXT: Certified: same [backend=Lean] [partial]
# BACKEND-NEXT: Certified: positive [backend=Lean] (its precondition is assumed, not checked, at calls from unverified unchecked)
# BACKEND-NEXT: {{.*}}lean_dependencies_backend.cpp:45:3: Unresolved: countdown [backend=Lean] [reason=decreases.missing] (the loop at 45:3 has no decreases clause
# BACKEND: warning: same: proved only for executions that terminate

# BACKEND-EXPORT: Exported: lean obligation: impossible
# BACKEND-EXPORT-NOT: warning: impossible

# BROKEN: Unresolved: lean obligation: impossible (Lean certification failed:
# BROKEN-NOT: warning: impossible

# INDUCTIVE: Unresolved: decreases: reach (Lean certification failed:

# BACKEND-JSON: "function":"seven"{{.*}}"reason":"callee.contract"{{.*}}"status":"unresolved"
# BACKEND-JSON: "function":"impossible"{{.*}}"status":"certified"{{.*}}"vacuous":true

# EXPORT: Exported: lean fallback: decreases: scaled [z3: 0 of 1 proved; lean: 1 exported]
# EXPORT: Unresolved: user [backend=z3] [reason=spec.termination]

# The termination proof does not certify, so the definition of scaled is
# not established, though another function failed.
# SORRY: Unresolved: lean fallback: decreases: scaled [z3: 0 of 1 proved; lean: 1 exported] (Lean certification failed:
# SORRY: Unresolved: user [backend=z3] [reason=spec.termination] (relies on the definition of scaled, whose termination is not established)
# SORRY: error: verification failed: wrong

# PROVED: Certified: decreases: scaled [backend=Lean]
# PROVED-NEXT: Verified: user [backend=z3]
# PROVED-NEXT: {{.*}}error: verification failed: wrong

# MIXED: Proved (z3+lean): product [z3: 1 of 2 proved; lean: 1 certified] [trusts=kept] (its precondition is assumed, not checked, at calls from unverified unchecked) [partial]
# MIXED-NEXT: Verified: six [backend=z3] [trusts=kept] [partial]
